@startuml component-reader-shell
!include elvira.iuml
' What: the reader shell is reduced to a page stream with one top bar and one Navigator drawer; every page draws its own layers, while the drawing canvas stays a single instance on the active page.
' Kind: UML component diagram. Scope: EvilFlowersViewer UI shell; the logic behind it is in component-viewer-architecture.puml.
' Source: src/components/PDFViewer.vue, src/components/pdf-viewer-page/*, src/stores/* (2026-11-18)

title Document-centric reader shell (implemented in #152)

component "PDFViewer.vue\n(root, controller)" as root
component "ReaderTopBar\n(title · page · search · ⋯)" as top
component "Navigator drawer\n(Contents · Pages · Search · Notes)" as nav
component "PageStream\n(continuous scroll, virtual window,\nkeyed per document)" as stream <<focus>>
component "PageView ×N\n(canvas · text · links · highlight layers\n· selection menu · explained passage)" as page
component "EditCanvas\n(single instance, teleported to the active page)" as edit
component "ChatPanel\n(right, host chat)" as chat
database "document store\n(activePage, navigation, history)" as docstore
database "search store" as search

root --> top : renders
root --> nav : renders
root --> stream : renders
root --> chat : renders when chatPackage
stream --> page : mounts pages in the window
stream -[$accent()]-> docstore : <b>activePage from scroll</b>\n(cause: scroll)
docstore --> stream : jumps (goTo) scroll the stream
page --> search : reads hits of its page
edit --> docstore : loads / saves by activePage
nav --> docstore : goTo(page, outline / search)
top --> docstore : page box, zoom, panels

caption One scroll container shows every page; layers are per page, the drawing canvas is one instance that follows the active page. The rail and the bottom bar are removed; their features move to the top bar, the Navigator and the ⋯ menu.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersViewer · docs/diagrams/component-reader-shell.puml
@enduml
